      "sample_index": 0,
      "text": "To find the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle, we need to follow these steps:\n\n1. **Find the complement of the 42-degree angle:**\n   - The complement of an angle is defined as the angle that, when added to the given angle, results in 90 degrees.\n   - Therefore, the complement of a 42-degree angle is:\n     \\[\n     90^\\circ - 42^\\circ = 48^\\circ\n     \\]\n\n2. **Find the supplement of the complement:**\n   - The supplement of an angle is defined as the angle that, when added to the given angle, results in 180 degrees.\n   - Therefore, the supplement of a 48-degree angle is:\n     \\[\n     180^\\circ - 48^\\circ = 132^\\circ\n     \\]\n\nThus, the degree measure of the supplement of the complement of a 42-degree angle is \\boxed{132}.",
